When compiling NetHack pl9 on a 4.3 BSD Dynix system, I run into the
following problem.  After making the appropriate changes in config.h,
unixconf.h, and the Makefiles, compilation complains at line 216 of
system.h:
E char *sprintf();
Redefinition problem, or something similar, and compilation proceeds
smoothly when I remove this line.
The major problem is that the screen display is fouled up:  floor
spaces and horizontal walls, monsters, objects on the floor that can
be picked up are all displayed normally.  Vertical walls, room features
such as fountains and staircases, wall sections (even horizontal ones)
that are actually secret doors, hallway spaces are not displayed
until I move on and off them, and intervening hallway spaces that
are traversed during a run with a shift-movement are still not displayed
afterwards.  All of these undisplayed squares appear as just blanks.

I suspect this problem is easily solved, but I'm not a knowledgeable
C programmer.  Trying to use different termcap libraries has been
about the extent of my experimentation.  Can anybody suggest
any changes I should make?

